{
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "the poet allows the ellipsis to remain because it is so easy to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "supply it. केचित्......केचित्-some...others. यं यं पश्यसि तस्य तस्य",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "पुरतः—before every one that you see. The fig. is अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "here.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 52. अकारणविग्रहः—causeless strife, unprovoked quarrel.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "इदम् refers to each of the foregoing nominatives.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 53. Every serpent of a particular species is supposed to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "have in its crest a jewel which shines by night. ‘ The verse is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "attributed to Chánakya. See Kâvyasangraha p. 293. and S'árng-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "adhara p. 63, ’ Telang. The fig. is दृष्टान्त by साधर्म्य. There is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "however a mixture of वस्तुप्रतिवस्तुभाव also.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 54. The language here is somewhat condensed. गुणः,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "दुर्जनैः and गण्यते have to be supplied with every clause. ह्रीमति यः",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ह्रीरूपः गुणः स जाड्यमिति गण्यते &c. व्रतरुचि—one who likes to stick",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "fast to religious observances. मुनि—ordinarily means मननशील",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "( from मन् + इन् the अ being changed to उ by Un. IV. 123 )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "one given to contemplation; hence here, a man of reserve, one",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "who keeps silence. ‘ वाचंयमो मुनिः ’ Amara. for the Vedántic",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "meaning see Bg. II. 56. quoted in the com. मुखरता—मुखरस्य",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "भावः । fr. मुख + र. The possessive aff. र here implies censure.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "नाम is used here संभाव्ये i. e. to express possibility; or it may",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "have the sense of ‘indeed.’ अङ्कितः—branded.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 55. लोभ—is regarded as the greatest of all evils being",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the origin of most of them. Cf. लोभः पापस्य कारणम् ’ H. I 27.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "see com. अगुण—Here the नञ् shows विरोध or opposition. निजैः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "If a man has सौजन्य his courteous conduct will easily win over",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "strangers and so there will be no lack of relatives to him where-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "ver he may go. धनैः—The other reading जनैः does not yield a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "good sense. Bhartṛhari considers Vidyá as the best treasure.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Cf. Sl. 16. 20. 21. and 103. अपयशः—Cf. Bg. II. 34.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "quoted in the com. न भीतोमरणादस्मि केवलं दूषितं यशः । Mṛch.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl.s 56. दिवसं०—दिवसेन ( Inst. हेतौ ) धूसरः rendered pale by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "( the overpowering light of ) day. अनक्षरम्—अविद्यमानमक्षरं यत्र तत् ।",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
